# Clinical Reasoning Language Example
library "Clinical Reasoning Language Example".

/*
Clinical Reasoning Language (CRL) — v0.7 grammar reference example.

Surface conventions:
  - Case sensitive (keywords are lowercase: `concept`, `defined as`, `definition is`,
    `sem-or`, `sem-and`, `sem-not`, `or`, `and`, `not`, etc.).
  - Whitespace insensitive (indentation is decorative).
  - File starts with `#` + markdown-valid header line.
  - Quoted strings (`"..."`) are identifiers / refs to named declarations.
  - Backtick strings (`` `...` ``) are free text / evidence / system / code.
  - Single quotes (`'...'`) lex as UCUM units inside Quantity literals.

Statement types:
  - decision     — reusable decision logic; when/then/recommend|use
  - terminology  — valueset reference OR system+code(s) pair
  - activity     — executable clinical activity (CPG resource request)
  - concept      — clinical concept; one of three body kinds:
                     - `coded from` (asserted; ref is a valueset)
                     - `defined as` (composition over named concept refs)
                     - `definition is` (catalog-matched narrative predicate)

`defined as` body shapes:
  - bare ref:        `- defined as "X".`
  - composition:     `- defined as ( "A" sem-and "B" ).` (uses sem-or/sem-and/sem-not)

Narrative inside a `definition is` body uses lowercase `or` / `and` for in-arg
disjunction (e.g. `("Medical Reasons" or "Patient Declined Reasons")`),
which is distinct from the `sem-or`/`sem-and` in concept composition.
See docs/CRL Compilation Pipeline.md and the
project_sem-composition-operators memory for the rationale.

Optional fields:
  - `meta is` (repeatable) and `evidence is` on `concept`
  - `with` and `because` on `activity`
  - `do not perform` suffix on `request` keyword (activity)
*/

decision "IMMZ.D2.D5.Measles":

- when "Measles Routine Immunization Schedule Incomplete" then:
  - when "No Primary Series Doses Administered" then:
    - when "Client Age Less Than 12 Months" then recommend activity "Indicate".
    - when "Last Live Vaccine Administered has had in 4 Weeks" then use decision "Elderly Based".
  - end when
- end when
- when "Client Is Due For MCV12" then recommend activity "Vaccinate".
- when "One Primary Series Dose Administered" then:
  any:
  - when "Client Age Less Than 15 Months" then recommend activity "Indicate".
  - when "Last Live Vaccine Administered has had in 4 Weeks" then use decision "Elderly Based".
  - when "Client Is Due For MCV12" then recommend activity "Vaccinate".
- end when
- when "Two Primary Series Doses Administered" then recommend activity "Indicate".

decision "Elderly Based":

- when "Client Age Greater Than 60" then recommend activity "Indicate".
- when "Client Age Less Than 60" then:
  all:
  - recommend activity "Vaccinate".
  - recommend activity "another thing".
  - recommend activity "something else".
- end when
- when "Client Age Greater Than 60" then:
  - when "Most Recent BMI" then:
    - use decision "Some Other Decision".
    - use decision "Some Other Other Decision".
  - end when
- end when


// ============ Activities ============

activity "Vaccinate":
- request CPGImmunizationRequest.

activity "Indicate":
- request CPGProposeDiagnosisTask.
- with "Colonoscopy".

activity "Message Care Plan":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Create a care plan`.
- because `A new plan needs to be implemented.`.

activity "Contraindicated":
- request do not perform CPGImmunizationRequest.
- with "Immunization".
- because `Immunization is contraindicated`.


// ============ Terminologies ============

terminology "BMI Range as a Condition":
- valueset is ``.

terminology "BMI as an Observation":
- valueset is `BMI as an Observation`.

terminology "Height Valueset":
- valueset is `height valueset`.

terminology "Weight Valueset":
- valueset is `weight valueset`.

terminology "Colonoscopy":
- system is `http://snomed.info/sct`.
- code is `73761001`.

terminology "Breast Cancer":
- system is `http://snomed.info/sct`.
- code is `73761002`.
- code is `73761003`.


// ============ Concepts ============

// --- Asserted concepts (coded from a terminology) ---

concept "BMI Range as a Condition":
- type is Condition.
- valuetype is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "BMI Range as a Condition".

concept "BMI as an Observation":
- type is Observation.
- valuetype is Quantity.
- coded from "BMI as an Observation".

concept "Patient Height":
- type is Observation.
- valuetype is integer.
- coded from "Height Valueset".

concept "Patient Weight":
- type is Observation.
- valuetype is integer.
- coded from "Weight Valueset".


// --- Composition concepts: bare ref + sem-* composition shapes ---

// "BMI" composes three sources via sem-or (semantic boolean — operands
// can be cross-typed; the composition layer reconciles).
concept "BMI":
- type is Observation.
- valuetype is Quantity.
- defined as
(
   "BMI Range as a Condition"
   sem-or
   "BMI as an Observation"
   sem-or
   "Calculated BMI"
).


// --- Predicate-kind concepts: narrative body + composing concept pair ---

// Predicates with narrative bodies are concepts with `definition is` bodies.
// A composing concept then references them as bare refs.

concept "Most Recent BMI Selection":
- meta is `Selects the most recent BMI observation within the configured lookback`.
- evidence is `Calculated by Smile`.
- definition is most recent "BMI".

concept "Most Recent BMI":
- type is Observation.
- valuetype is Quantity.
- meta is `Some meta information`.
- evidence is `Calculated by Smile`.
- defined as "Most Recent BMI Selection".

concept "Calculated BMI Formula":
- evidence is `Standard BMI formula: weight (kg) / height (m)^2`.
- definition is calculated "BMI".

concept "Calculated BMI":
- type is Observation.
- valuetype is Quantity.
- defined as "Calculated BMI Formula".


// --- Composition concepts: with sem-not ---

// `sem-not` is prefix unary; it negates the following operand or group.
// "BMI With Confirmed Height-Weight Source" requires BMI from a calculated
// source, NOT from a coded condition entry.
concept "BMI With Confirmed Height-Weight Source":
- type is Observation.
- valuetype is Quantity.
- defined as
(
   "Calculated BMI"
   sem-and
   sem-not "BMI Range as a Condition"
).

// For more complex composition examples (deeply nested groups, AND NOT,
// in-arg disjunctions inside narrative bodies), see the modeled measures:
//   features/cql-pattern-mining/results/models/cms22.crl
//   features/cql-pattern-mining/results/models/cms69.crl
